!!id:"https://tson.io/test-suite/class2/schema/invalid/an-enum-member-that-is-not-a-name-expected.tn"
!!schema:"https://tson.io/test-suite/schemas/schema-sidecar.tn"
{
  spec: "[TSON-SCHEMA] §7.4, [TSON-DATA] §7.7"
  description: """
    `enum` pins `name_type: identifier`, so every member must be an identifier -- a value of [TSON-DATA]
    §7.7's grammar. `lightly active` holds a space, so it is not a name and the enum contradicts its
    own type: a schema-load error, in the family of coherence errors §7.2 makes a compilation concern
    rather than data validation.

    The companion valid vector writes the same member set as an `enum_type` over the author's own
    identifier type, whose profile admits a single space between words, and resolves. What this one guards is that `enum` is the strict reading: a processor admitting
    any text under `!enum` would accept this document and would, in doing so, have dropped §8.2's
    restricted-character and restricted-script rules from every enum in existence without anything
    being written down.
    """
  meta: "meta.tn"
  import: ["core.tn"]
  error: {
    category: resolver
  }
}
